# Bot1 has two Mistrise Villages and activates both on turn 5 before casting anything, then casts two Lightning Bolts at
# Bot2, who counters each. Each activation is its own effect "the next spell you cast this turn" (CR 611.2c): both
# apply to the same next spell, the first Bolt, and both are used up by it. So the first Bolt resists its Counterspell and
# the second, cast with no effect left, is countered. If the second effect had waited for the second Bolt, both would resolve.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Mox Ruby
Mistrise Village
Lightning Bolt
Lightning Bolt
Mistrise Village
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Counterspell
Counterspell
Forest x14

